``ts\nconst cursedSurcharge = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  item.cursed ? BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] * 0.5 : 0;\n\nconst cursedSurchargeSum = mainItems.reduce(\n  (sum, item) => sum + cursedSurcharge(item),\n  0\n);\n```\n\n- Constants: 1 (`0.5`) + 1 (`0` init) = 2\n- Bindings: 5 (`cursedSurcharge`, `item`, `cursedSurchargeSum`, `sum`, `item` in reduce)\n- Invocations: 4 (`cursedSurcharge()` call, `reduce`, `*`, `+`) = mass 8\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary `? :`) = mass 4\n- Loops: 1 (`reduce`) = mass 5\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 2 + 5 + 8 + 4 + 5 + 0 = **24**\n\nMass Change: 21 -> 24 (delta +3)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Renamed `itemModifiers` -> `cursedSurchargeSum`; extracted the inline `if` into a named `cursedSurcharge(item)` function. This directly names the domain concept from the spec (\"item-specific modifiers apply to the base premium of the affected item\") instead of a vague plural.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) takes priority over Rule 4 (Fewest Elements) here: extracting the named helper costs +3 mass (one extra binding/invocation), but the surcharge rule now reads as a single expression matching the spec's own vocabulary, and it gives a natural seam for the upcoming high-enchantment surcharge test (`it.todo` already anticipates a second item-specific modifier) without needing another rename right away.\n- No duplication or over-engineering introduced: only one helper was extracted, no premature generalization for the not-yet-implemented enchantment surcharge.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `itemModifiers` -> `cursedSurchargeSum` and extracted `cursedSurcharge(item)` helper to reveal the domain concept per spec language.\n**Mass Change**: 21 -> 24 (+3, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 5 passing tests still green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-51-45_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added item-scoped cursed surcharge (50% of the affected item's own base premium, per spec: \"item-specific modifiers apply to the base premium of the affected item\"). This is computed separately from the policy-wide first-insurance surcharge (10% of the policy base sum) and added after the 10% multiplication, not before, since the spec says item-specific surcharges apply to the item's base premium, not the policy base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: NODE_ENV must be set to \"development\" for `pnpm test` to work in this sandbox, e.g. `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added item-scoped cursed surcharge (50% of the affected item's own base premium, per spec: \"item-specific modifiers apply to the base premium of the affected item\"). This is computed separately from the policy-wide first-insurance surcharge (10% of the policy base sum) and added after the 10% multiplication, not before, since the spec says item-specific surcharges apply to the item's base premium, not the policy base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: NODE_ENV must be set to \"development\" for `pnpm test` to work in this sandbox, e.g. `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784916623243},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01LFwcahEWkEkc5QMgnhjBVt","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KmuV3fEyhU3NYsjqvtFm4F","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":342,"output":121,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10231,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916623263,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cd28b9be-1a91-44e0-9509-b8aca9aa9e51","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01LFwcahEWkEkc5QMgnhjBVt","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteCustomer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteInput {\n  customer: QuoteCustomer;\n  items: QuoteItem[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_OF_3_PREMIUM = 60;\n\n// Rounds up to the nearest whole gold, avoiding floating-point artifacts\n// like 100 * 1.1 = 110.00000000000001 by rounding to 6 decimals first.\nconst roundUpToWholeGold = (amount: number): number => {\n  return Math.ceil(Math.round(amount * 1e6) / 1e6);\n};\n\nexport const calculatePremium = (input: QuoteInput): number => {\n  if (input.items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  }\n\n  const componentPremium = (count: number): number => {\n    if (count === 3) {\n      return COMPONENT_BLOCK_OF_3_PREMIUM;\n    }\n    return count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  };\n\n  const isComponent = (item: QuoteItem) => COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type);\n  const componentItems = input.items.filter(isComponent);\n  const mainItems = input.items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n\n  const componentsSum = COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = componentItems.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    return sum + componentPremium(count);\n  }, 0);\n\n  const policyBaseSum =\n    componentsSum +\n    mainItems.reduce((sum, item) => sum + BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type], 0);\n\n  const itemModifiers = mainItems.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      return sum + BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] * 0.5;\n    }\n    return sum;\n  }, 0);\n\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBaseSum * 1.1 + itemModifiers;\n  const total = withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return roundUpToWholeGold(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916625275},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01KmuV3fEyhU3NYsjqvtFm4F","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { calculatePremium } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Quote premium calculation\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const premium = calculatePremium({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, items: [] });\n    expect(premium).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  it(\"each main item type priced from the MHPCO price list for a newcomer's first contract -> sword 115 G, amulet 71 G, staff 93 G, potion 49 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] })).toBe(115);\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] })).toBe(71);\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] })).toBe(93);\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] })).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  it(\"components without a block: block requires exactly 3 alike components -> 2 runes 60 G, 4 runes 115 G, 7 runes 198 G (rounded up)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const runes = (n: number) => Array.from({ length: n }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: runes(2) })).toBe(60);\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: runes(4) })).toBe(115);\n    expect(calculatePremium({ customer, items: runes(7) })).toBe(198);\n  });\n\n  it(\"alike components are grouped by type only -> 2 runes + 1 moonstone 88 G (no block); 3 runes + 3 moonstones 137 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(\n      calculatePremium({\n        customer,\n        items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n      })\n    ).toBe(88);\n    expect(\n      calculatePremium({\n        customer,\n        items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        ],\n      })\n    ).toBe(137);\n  });\n\n  it(\"Newcomer with a cursed sword integration example -> premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const premium = calculatePremium({\n      customer,\n      items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n    });\n    expect(premium).toBe(165);\n  });\n\n  it.todo(\n    \"high-enchantment surcharge applies at enchantment >= 5 -> enchant 4: 115 G (no surcharge), enchant 5: 145 G, enchant 5 + cursed: 195 G (both surcharges)\"\n  );\n\n  it.todo(\n    \"loyalty discount applies for customers with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> premium 95 G for a single sword\"\n  );\n\n  it.todo(\n    \"Long-standing customer's second contract integration example -> premium 160 G (first-insurance surcharge always applies per item; follow-up discount also applies)\"\n  );\n\n  it.todo(\n    \"modifier scope on multi-item policy: item-specific surcharges scope to the item's base premium, policy-wide modifiers scope to the policy base premium -> cursed sword + amulet, newcomer/first contract = 231 G\"\n  );\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916625275},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_011eWfbpLo2dL1qKBUAASAUH