acheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784917258575,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-75f2ea07-cf5d-4b08-8524-2d535a2968f7","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Jow2HUjtjhhYSGpKrztpaK","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 8 tests still pass.\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- **Naming**: Renamed `policySumBeforeLoyaltyDiscount` → `policySumBeforeDiscounts` and updated its comment. The old name became stale/misleading once the follow-up-contract discount was added in this Green phase — the variable is now consumed by *two* discount subtractions, not just the loyalty one, so the old name no longer revealed accurate intent.\n- **Mass**: Unchanged (18 → 18) — this was a pure rename, so mass is identical. Rule 2 (clarity) took priority even though APP mass wasn't reduced, per \"Rule 2 trumps APP.\"\n- **Rule 3 (duplication) considered and rejected**: `loyaltyDiscount` and `followUpDiscount` are structurally similar (`condition ? policyBaseSum * RATE : 0`), but they represent two distinct, independently-toggleable business rules with different names and conditions. Merging them into a combined-rate calculation would save a few mass points but would obscure which discount is which — clarity loss outweighs the minor DRY gain, so I kept them separate.\n\n## APP Mass Comparison (relevant slice)\n- Before: 18\n- After: 18\n- Delta: 0 (rename only; no structural mass change)\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `policySumBeforeLoyaltyDiscount` to `policySumBeforeDiscounts` to accurately reflect that it now precedes both the loyalty and follow-up-contract discounts (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent). Considered merging the two discount calculations (Rule 3) but rejected it as it would reduce clarity for a distinct business rule.\n**Mass Change**: 18 -> 18 (no change; clarity-only fix)\n**Tests**: All 8 tests passing (1 todo, unaffected)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAge