LD` ref (treat literal-like refs ~2 relevant: `0`) = 1\n- Invocations: `??` (1, nullish coalescing) = 2\n- Conditionals: `if`, `&&`, `>=` (3) = 12\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: `reimbursement = ...` (initial) + `reimbursement = ...` (reassignment inside if) = 2 assignments = 12\n\nTotal ≈ 1 + 4 + 2 + 12 + 0 + 12 = **31**\n\n**Rule 2 Evaluation (Reveals Intent)**: The `let` + reassignment pattern requires the reader to track mutation across two locations. The condition also lacks a name explaining *why* the branch exists (the \"high-enchantment clause\"). This hurts intent-revealing more than it helps.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Extracted `hasHighEnchantmentClause` as a named boolean, and replaced the `let`/`if`-reassignment with a single `const` ternary expression.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nconst hasHighEnchantmentClause =\n  item !== undefined && (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\nconst reimbursement = hasHighEnchantmentClause\n  ? firstDamage.amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE\n  : firstDamage.amount;\nconst payout = reimbursement - DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD;\n```\n- Bindings: `hasHighEnchantmentClause`, `reimbursement`, `payout`, `item`, `firstDamage` (5) = 5\n- Constants: `0` (1) = 1\n- Invocations: `??` (1) = 2\n- Conditionals: `!==`, `&&`, `>=`, `?:` (4) = 16\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0 (all `const`, no reassignment) = 0\n\nTotal ≈ 1 + 5 + 2 + 16 + 0 + 0 = **24**\n\n**Mass Change**: 31 → 24 (Δ −7)\n\n**Benefits**:\n- Eliminated mutable state (`let` → all `const`), removing 2 assignment-mass units (12 mass) entirely\n- The named condition `hasHighEnchantmentClause` documents *why* the branch exists, directly matching the domain language already used in comments/tests (\"high-enchantment clause\")\n- Rule 3 (duplication): checked — no duplication with `quote.ts`'s similar high-enchantment logic; different domain (surcharge vs. reimbursement, different thresholds/rates), so no extraction warranted (would hurt clarity per Rule 2)\n- Rule 4 (fewest elements): no unnecessary abstractions introduced; single well-named boolean is justified by intent clarity\n\n**Tests**: All 3 active tests passing (12 total passing including quote.spec.ts, 9 claim tests still `it.todo`).\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Replaced `let`/reassignment pattern with a named boolean (`hasHighEnchantmentClause`) + ternary `const` expression in `calculatePayout`\n**Mass Change**: 31 → 24 (Δ −7)\n**Tests**: All passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-51-45_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added item lookup (find the policy item matching the first damage's itemType) and applied a 50% reimbursement rate (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE) when the item's enchantment is >= 8 (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD), before subtracting the deductible.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: NODE_ENV must be set to \"development\" for `pnpm test` to work in this sandbox, e.g. `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added item lookup (find the policy item matching the first damage's itemType) and applied a 50% reimbursement rate (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE) when the item's enchantment is >= 8 (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD), before subtracting the deductible.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Note: NODE_ENV must be set to \"development\" for `pnpm test` to work in this sandbox, e.g. `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return wh